{"version":1,"content":"\n<p>粉嶺皇后山深處，穿過陡峭山坡和鐵絲網，有一座遺世獨立的印度廟。以蓮花為概念設計的六角尖頂建築，曾是上世紀駐港尼泊爾啹喀兵（Gurkha）的聖地。90 年代英軍逐步撤出香港，皇后山軍營人去樓空，廟宇隨之荒廢近 30 年，雜草叢生、牆身剝落。直至近年，在港尼泊爾社群自發籌款、動手修葺，並每日輪流清潔，方讓這座三級歷史建築逐漸回復昔日光華。<br/><br/>昨日（10月25日）午後，平日靜謐的廟宇人聲鼎沸。近 40 位信眾幾代同堂，女士身穿傳統服飾、戴上花飾與手鐲，男士則有啹喀第三代年輕人特地穿上軍服亮相，一同慶祝尼泊爾最盛大的節日——德賽節（Dashain）的最後一日滿月日（Kojagrat Purnima），為長達 15 日的慶典畫上句號。廟外綠樹成蔭、經幡飄揚，綠色尖頂建築在陽光下格外醒目；廟內則紅繩、花環與銅鈴交錯，香氣縈繞。<br/><br/>儀式中，家族女性長輩為後輩在眉心點上由朱砂、乳酪和米混合而成的 Tika，耳朵插上青草 Jamara，並往頭上撒米，象徵力量與保護女神難近母（Durga）的庇佑，祈求豐收、健康與好運。有母親抱著幼兒接受祝福，也有年輕人低頭領受長輩的點額。<br/><br/>祭司 Narayan 帶領信眾圍坐誦讀、吟唱《吠陀經》（Vedas），燃點聖火，把米拋向火焰供奉神明；地上鋪着紅布，擺滿水果、米與供品。部分信眾改以澆灌聖木（holy tree）代替傳統牲畜獻祭，象徵祈福與慈悲。<br/><br/>適逢尼泊爾水災後的第一次德賽節。有信眾表示，即使身處異地，仍對祖國念茲在茲，相信光明終會驅走黑暗，正義終會戰勝邪惡。這座曾被遺忘的「啹喀廟」，經社群多年自發修葺與每日清潔，再次凝聚在港尼泊爾人，成為他們共同的精神家園。</p>\n<p></p>\n<figure><img alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"683\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/20261025_nepal_QueensHill-1-1024x683.jpeg\" width=\"1024\"/></figure>\n<p></p>\n<figure><img alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"683\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/20261025_nepal_QueensHill-2-1024x683.jpeg\" width=\"1024\"/></figure>\n<p></p>\n<figure><img alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"683\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/20261025_nepal_QueensHill-3-1024x683.jpeg\" width=\"1024\"/></figure>\n<p></p>\n<figure><img alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"683\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/20261025_nepal_QueensHill-4-1024x683.jpeg\" width=\"1024\"/></figure>\n<p></p>\n<figure><img alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"683\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/20261025_nepal_QueensHill-5-1024x683.jpeg\" width=\"1024\"/></figure>\n<p></p>\n<figure><img alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"683\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/20261025_nepal_QueensHill-6-1024x683.jpeg\" width=\"1024\"/></figure>\n<p></p>\n<figure><img alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"683\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/20261025_nepal_QueensHill-7-1024x683.jpeg\" width=\"1024\"/></figure>\n<p></p>\n<figure><img alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"683\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/20261025_nepal_QueensHill-8-1024x683.jpeg\" width=\"1024\"/></figure>\n<p></p>\n<figure><img alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"683\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/20261025_nepal_QueensHill-9-1024x683.jpeg\" width=\"1024\"/></figure>\n<p></p>\n<figure><img alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"683\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/20261025_nepal_QueensHill-10-1024x683.jpeg\" width=\"1024\"/></figure>\n<p></p>\n<figure><img alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"237\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/Payme-500x237.png\" width=\"500\"/></figure>\n","scraped_at":"2026-10-26T04:46:34.372662+00:00","quality":{"score":2,"chars":694,"images":11,"source":"The Collective HK","fallback":"rss-http-error","origin":"wordpress-public-posts","completeness":"unverified"},"published_at":"2026-10-26T04:15:13+00:00","fetched_at":"2026-10-27T08:58:21.360448+00:00","content_updated_at":"2026-10-26T04:40:19.352117+00:00","content_hash":"d918e92f7a7548ac03215b28fd5aa6241e929855c10a95c800d1425ac63347a4","evidence_status":"partial","scrape_error":"HTTP 520","content_retention":null,"content_capture":null}